          "title": "You'll want to know: interpeller",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "interpeller — \"to stop and question (police); to call out to\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "La police a interpellé deux jeunes hommes. The police stopped two young men for questioning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In the news, interpeller means the police took someone in. In the street, it means to call out to someone."
            }
          ]
        },
